[h1]Speculative Markets[/h1]
When a good's price keeps rising, investors pile in. Sometimes they overdo it, and the boom ends in a crash. This mod brings booms, manias, bank credit and financial panics to Victoria 3, gives every country a stock exchange that competes with the world's, and gives you the tools to manage it all.

[list]
[*]Built and tested on game version 1.15.1
[*]Works in a running campaign, and with saves from earlier versions
[/list]

Upcoming changes are tested in [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275304]Speculative Markets - Beta[/url] before reaching this stable release. Enable stable or Beta, never both.

[h2]The Finance panel[/h2]
Everything lives in one new panel. Open it with the Finance button on the left of the screen. It has four tabs, laid out like the game's own panels. Hover anything to see why it is what it is.

[h2]Exchange[/h2]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/uU0sfan.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Your Exchange[/b] rises from Provincial to National, International and World Centre as its score grows. Each rise opens another Speciality.
[*][b]Exchange Charter.[/b] Pick one: a Commodity Exchange for hotter booms, a Money Market for steadier trust, or a Share Market for more credit.
[*][b]Paths to Renown.[/b] Choose Specialities and compete with the world's Exchanges on each one. The higher you place, the more it gives.
[/list]

[h2]Speculation[/h2]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/NiNIlhY.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Market Confidence[/b], from 0 to 100. Booms push it up. Crashes, losing wars and debt pull it down. Above 80, investors get reckless. Below the Panic Threshold, a Financial Panic begins: output and taxes fall, the treasury pays relief for the jobless, banks call in loans and private construction is cut in half.
[*][b]Investor Interest[/b] in every good, from Fleeing to Feverish. Hot goods attract more investment, and the hotter the boom, the harder it can end.
[*][b]Your levers.[/b] Restrain a hot good, encourage a slow one, or float a Great Issue to raise your Exchange score, and the stakes.
[/list]

[h2]Banking[/h2]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/8ob11sb.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Credit Leverage.[/b] Bank credit speeds up your economy: each month of leverage adds 2% throughput, up to 24%. Past 3 months a panic starts sooner and leaves Bad Debts, which cut throughput and investment for years.
[*][b]Lending Limit.[/b] How far banks can lend, from 3 months of investment pool income up to 12 with the finance technologies and a leading Exchange.
[*][b]Credit Policy.[/b] Tight, Normal or Loose: how freely your banks lend.
[*][b]Bank Rescue.[/b] Lend to the Banks to shorten a panic and reduce its output, tax and private-construction penalties; ongoing relief expenses continue. Buy up bad loans afterwards, or pledge in advance to rescue every panic at once, for less.
[/list]

[h2]Rankings[/h2]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/kfYbzHP.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Leading Exchanges.[/b] Every Exchange of National Standing or higher, ranked by score. The top five gain prestige, cheaper loans and a higher Lending Limit.
[*][b]Rival Exchange.[/b] Name a rival at or above your score. Each year the higher score takes trust from the other.
[/list]

[h2]Around the world[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Panics spread.[/b] A Great Power's crash can hit its trading partners and the countries whose economies it owns. From around 1870 it can start a worldwide Long Depression.
[*][b]A world market map.[/b] Open the Financial Markets journal entry to see every country's market by stage, with stripes where a panic has just spread.
[*][b]Laws matter.[/b] Each economic system and trade policy law lists what it does to the markets in its own tooltip. Under Command Economy or Cooperative Ownership, investors do not speculate at all.
[*][b]Alerts[/b] under the top bar warn you when a panic is close or a bubble has built up.
[/list]
For a wilder ride, set the Market Volatility game rule to High.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Community Mod Framework:[/b] use the separate [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275348]Speculative Markets - CMF Compatibility patch[/url]. Set the order manually: CMF, this mod (or Beta), then the patch last. Enable only one Speculative Markets channel.
[*]Changes the goods panel and the left-side information panel bar, and adds investor effects to industry, farm, mine, plantation, port, whaling and art academy building definitions. Mods that replace those GUI files or the same building definitions may need a compatibility patch.
[*]In multiplayer, every player needs the mod.
[*]Available in English, Brazilian Portuguese, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Spanish and Turkish. The other languages are machine translated, so corrections are welcome.
[/list]

