[h2]Updates[/h2]
[b]1.0.3[/b] Fixes a crash when displaying boom-ending notifications. Banking and overbuilding details are captured safely for each notification. No balance changes.
[b]1.0.2[/b] Fixes the Financial Markets journal and goods-panel Open Finance shortcuts. They now open Finance directly on the Speculation tab.
[b]1.0.1[/b] Fixes: panic relief and depression penalties now end when markets close, and affected saves are repaired. Exchanges and rankings stay correct after annexations, old events no longer restart closed markets, and new buildings get investor effects. The Finance panel closes when another opens, its filters work properly, and panic tooltips show the output and tax penalties.
[b]1.0.0[/b] New: the Finance panel, with Exchange, Speculation, Banking and Rankings tabs. Every country now has an Exchange with a Standing, a Charter and Specialities, and competes with the world's on the Paths to Renown and against a Rival Exchange. Float a Great Issue on a hot good. Pledge to Rescue the Banks. New charts: where the banks have lent, Credit Leverage History, and trade by Investor Interest. Banks now track which goods they lend into, so a boom they financed ends harder. Panics hit harder: every building's output and the taxes collected fall, relief for the jobless costs the treasury every week, and a Bank Rescue costs more. The Lending Limit now tops out at 12 months, the Panic Threshold rises with leverage, and Bad Debts grow steadily with how hard a panic hits. Clearer, shorter tooltips throughout.
